{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"youtube","name":"Ad-free YouTube","version":"0.3.1","apiVersion":1,"description":"Samsung's own YouTube with ads blocked, Shorts hidden and sponsors skipped (TizenTube). Local proxy; fetches one pinned script from cdn.jsdelivr.net.","author":"andrearicci93","permissions":["exec"],"ui":{"label":"Ad-free YouTube"}},"files":{"README.md":"# Ad-free YouTube\n\nSamsung's own YouTube app on your TV, **without ads**. The plugin opens the YouTube app that is already on the TV and adds\na script to its page: ads blocked, Shorts hidden, sponsor segments skipped ([SponsorBlock](https://sponsor.ajay.app)),\noptional [DeArrow](https://dearrow.ajay.app) titles. You stay signed in, voice search and the TV's player keep working, and\n**nothing is installed on the TV**: no WGT, no Developer mode, no re-signing, no second YouTube app.\n\n## What you get\n\n- Ads blocked before and inside videos, as far as the script keeps up with YouTube (see *Limits*).\n- Shorts removed from the menu, SponsorBlock skipping, optional DeArrow titles and thumbnails.\n- Your own account, history and subscriptions: it is the real YouTube app, not a clone.\n- An optional switch so Samsung's own YouTube button (Home tile, remote key, voice) opens the patched app.\n- If anything fails (proxy down, script missing, certificate missing) YouTube still opens, just without the patches.\n\n## Install and use\n\n1. In the dashboard open **Vetro Shards → Load plugin catalog**, find **Ad-free YouTube** and install it. It lands switched off.\n2. Switch it on, open its tab, press **Open YouTube**. The first start takes up to a minute: it makes a certificate, copies the\n   YouTube app's content folder (about 3 MB) and downloads the script once.\n3. Optional: switch on **Samsung's YouTube button opens this** (see *The Home tile*).\n\n**Remove it cleanly:** switch the tile option off, press **Remove certificate and files**, switch the plugin off, then remove\nit. Removing the plugin alone leaves the certificate and the copy of the content folder on the TV.\n\n**Tested on:** a Samsung Q80A (firmware 2310.0, Tizen 6.0) rooted with Vetro. Other models should work if they have the Cobalt\nYouTube app (`com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt`); the plugin says \"Samsung YouTube not found\" when they do not. Not yet confirmed:\nthe real remote YouTube key after a cold boot, and long-term behaviour as YouTube changes.\n\n## How it works\n\nThe YouTube app on the TV is Cobalt (`com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt`). It accepts a proxy and a content folder on its command line.\nThe plugin starts it with both:\n\n```\napp_launcher -s com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt -u 5001 USERDATA ' --base_url=https://www.youtube.com/tv --dial_name=YouTube --use_eden --start_frag=#start --proxy=127.0.0.2:8101,direct:// --content=/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vyt'\n```\n\n- **The first four flags** are the ones Samsung's own YouTube tile passes. The proxy list ends in `direct://`: if the proxy is\n  down, the app connects directly (unpatched) instead of failing.\n- **The proxy** runs inside Vetro, on `127.0.0.2` only. Every host is a plain tunnel except `www.youtube.com`, whose start page\n  gets one `<script>` tag. If the certificate or the script is missing, the proxy only tunnels: YouTube then runs unpatched\n  instead of breaking.\n- **The certificate.** The plugin makes a certificate authority of its own and adds it to a *copy* of the YouTube app's content\n  folder (`/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vyt`, a short path on purpose: see *The Home tile*). Only the YouTube app started by this plugin trusts it. The TV's trust store is never touched, and\n  `ca.key` is readable by root only, and `<DIR>` itself belongs to root: the only folder the apps' user can write in is\n  `<DIR>/cache` (the downloaded script, checked by hash on every read), so it cannot swap a file for a link that a root command follows.\n- **The script** is [TizenTube](https://github.com/reisxd/TizenTube) (reisxd, GPL-3.0), one exact release, downloaded from\n  npm's CDN on first use and used only if its SHA-256 matches the one in the plugin. It is not part of this plugin. Sponsor\n  segments come from the public [SponsorBlock](https://sponsor.ajay.app) database (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).\n\n`<DIR>` is `/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vetro-youtube`.\n\n## After a boot\n\nSamsung removes the wrapper app behind the YouTube key from the TV's app list at every boot, so the tile row cannot be patched\nuntil Samsung brings it back. While **Samsung's YouTube button opens this** is on, the plugin therefore checks every 6 seconds\nwhether YouTube was started without its proxy flags and, if so, closes it and starts it again through the proxy (at most 3 times\nin 2 minutes). At boot it also retries the first jobs every 3 seconds until Vetro's root agent has connected. Nothing is installed.\n\n## The Home tile (optional, off by default)\n\nSamsung's tile, remote key and voice all start the wrapper app `9Ur5IzDKqV.TizenYouTube`, which reads its flags from one row of\nthe web app service's database (`/opt/dbspace/.webappservice.db`, table `widgetinfo`, column `reserved_string_6`). The same text also\nsits in the app's `config.xml` and in the package database, but neither is read when the app starts (checked on a Q80A). The switch\nappends `--proxy=127.0.0.2:<port>,direct:// --content=/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vyt` to that row with the `sqlite3` command, and\ntakes it out again. The rules:\n\n- **The TV passes the app at most 127 characters of that value** (it cuts the rest silently, so the app would start without\n  `--content`, not trust the plugin's certificate, and show a white screen). Samsung's value is 88 characters, so the plugin\n  takes out `--base_url=https://www.youtube.com/tv` (the address the app uses anyway when it is not given) and puts it back in front\n  when it restores. That is why the content folder has a short path, and why a value that would not fit is left alone.\n- The row is patched only while the proxy is listening and the certificate and script are ready; otherwise (and when the switch\n  goes off, when the plugin is switched off, when Vetro stops, and on *Remove certificate and files*) it is put back.\n  All changes to the row go through one queue, so a slow patch can never land after a restore. A failed restore is retried.\n- Each write only happens if the row still holds what was read (compare-and-swap); only that row of that one app is touched;\n  values with quotes, `$`, backticks or non-ASCII text are never written.\n- Our two flags are removed wherever they sit in the value, so a firmware that adds its own flag after them does not strand them.\n  If our flags are in a value this plugin will not edit, *Remove certificate and files* refuses and deletes nothing.\n- If Vetro dies without restoring the row, YouTube still opens (the proxy list ends in `direct://`), unpatched.\n\n## Commands it runs, all as root and only when you press a button\n\n- Open: `openssl` (make or renew the authority and the youtube.com certificate), `cp -R` of the YouTube app's content folder\n  (about 3 MB), `app_launcher -t` and `app_launcher -s` for `com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt`.\n- Close: `app_launcher -t com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt`.\n- The Home tile switch: `sqlite3` on that database (read the one row, compare-and-swap update), then `chown` of the database back to its owner.\n- Remove certificate and files: puts the row back, closes YouTube and runs `rm -rf <DIR>`.\n\nSwitching the plugin off stops the proxy but does not close a YouTube that is already open: connections already made keep\nworking and new ones fall back to a direct connection.\nRemoving the plugin does **not** remove `<DIR>`: press *Remove certificate and files* first.\n\n## Limits\n\n- Every request to youtube.com goes through a new TLS connection, so the TV does a bit more work than with the plain app.\n- A new TizenTube release needs a new version of this plugin (the hash is pinned on purpose).\n- Ads inside videos depend on the script keeping up with YouTube; if they come back, the script needs updating, not the plugin.\n- Unofficial, and YouTube's terms do not allow ad blocking. Use it on your own TV, at your own risk.\n- Port 8101 can be changed with `{\"port\": 8123}` in the plugin's `config.json`.\n\n## Privacy: what it connects to\n\n- `cdn.jsdelivr.net` once, to download the TizenTube script (checked by SHA-256 before use). Nothing is sent but the request.\n- `www.youtube.com`: the proxy forwards the app's own requests; it reads the start page to add the script tag and keeps nothing.\n- The script, running inside YouTube's page, talks to YouTube and to the SponsorBlock / DeArrow servers (sponsor.ajay.app,\n  dearrow.ajay.app) the way TizenTube does. This plugin collects nothing and sends nothing anywhere else.\n\n## Credits\n\nThis plugin is only the glue. The hard parts are other people's work:\n\n- **[TizenTube](https://github.com/reisxd/TizenTube)** by **reisxd** (GPL-3.0): the script that blocks the ads, and the discovery\n  that Cobalt accepts `--proxy` and `--content`, which this whole approach is built on. The script is downloaded from its npm\n  package (`@foxreis/tizentube`) and is not part of this plugin.\n- **[SponsorBlock](https://github.com/ajayyy/SponsorBlock)** and **[DeArrow](https://github.com/ajayyy/DeArrow)** by **Ajay\n  Ramachandran** and contributors: the community database of sponsor segments (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) and of titles and thumbnails.\n- **Cobalt**, Google's open-source YouTube client that Samsung ships as the TV's YouTube app.\n- **[Vetro](https://github.com/andrearicci93/vetro)** for the plugin host, and Samsung's `sqlite3`, `openssl` and\n  `app_launcher` for the rest.\n\n## Legal\n\nUnofficial and not affiliated with Google, YouTube, Samsung, TizenTube or SponsorBlock. YouTube's terms of service do not\nallow ad blocking; use it on your own TV, at your own risk. This plugin is MIT-licensed like the rest of this catalog; the\nTizenTube script it downloads keeps its own GPL-3.0 licence.\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Ad-free YouTube: opens Samsung's own YouTube app with a script added to its page (ad blocking, Shorts, SponsorBlock, DeArrow).\n// Nothing is installed on the TV: the app is started with a proxy and a trust store of its own, both owned by this plugin.\n// See README.md for what runs, what is written, and how to undo it. Plain ES5.\n//\n// Two ways in: the Open button, and (when switched on) Samsung's own YouTube button, by adding the same flags to the row\n// that tile reads (tile.js). The row is only ever patched while everything it needs is up, and is put back when anything is\n// not, when the plugin is switched off, and when Vetro stops. If Vetro dies without a chance to do that, the proxy list ends\n// in direct:// so YouTube still opens.\n\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar path = require('path');\nvar proxyLib = require('./proxy.js');\nvar setup = require('./setup.js');\nvar tile = require('./tile.js');\nvar scriptLib = require('./userscript.js');\n\nvar PROXY_HOST = '127.0.0.2', DEFAULT_PORT = 8101;\nvar TICK_MS = 60 * 1000, SETUP_EVERY_MS = 24 * 3600 * 1000, SCRIPT_RETRY_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000, WATCH_MS = 6000;\n\nvar PAGE = '<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">' +\n    '<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">' +\n    '<style>body{font:15px system-ui;margin:16px;max-width:42rem}h2{margin:0 0 4px}.row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:14px 0}' +\n    'button{font:inherit;padding:8px 14px}table{border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px 0;width:100%}td{padding:4px 8px 4px 0;vertical-align:top}' +\n    'td:first-child{opacity:.7;white-space:nowrap}#msg{min-height:1.4em;margin:8px 0}.err{color:#c0392b}small{opacity:.75;display:block;margin-top:14px;line-height:1.45}' +\n    'label.sw{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;margin:14px 0 4px}label.sw input{margin-top:3px;width:18px;height:18px}#tilenote{opacity:.75;margin:0 0 8px 28px;min-height:1.2em}</style>' +\n    '<body><h2>Ad-free YouTube</h2><div>Samsung’s own YouTube app, with ads, Shorts and sponsor segments handled.</div>' +\n    '<div class=\"row\"><button id=\"open\">Open YouTube</button><button id=\"close\">Close YouTube</button></div><div id=\"msg\"></div>' +\n    '<label class=\"sw\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"tile\"><span><b>Samsung’s YouTube button opens this</b><br>The Home tile, the remote’s YouTube key and voice start the patched app. ' +\n    'If Vetro is not running, YouTube still opens, just without the patches.</span></label><div id=\"tilenote\"></div>' +\n    '<table><tr><td>Certificate</td><td id=\"s_setup\">…</td></tr><tr><td>Script</td><td id=\"s_script\">…</td></tr>' +\n    '<tr><td>Proxy</td><td id=\"s_proxy\">…</td></tr><tr><td>Pages patched</td><td id=\"s_pages\">…</td></tr></table>' +\n    '<div class=\"row\"><button id=\"clean\">Remove certificate and files</button></div>' +\n    '<small>The first start makes a certificate that only this YouTube app trusts (the TV does not) and downloads the script once, ' +\n    'checked against a fixed SHA-256. The script is <b>TizenTube</b> by reisxd (GPL-3.0); sponsor segments come from the ' +\n    '<b>SponsorBlock</b> database (sponsor.ajay.app, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). Unofficial: YouTube’s terms do not allow ad blocking.</small>' +\n    '<script>' +\n    'function $(i){return document.getElementById(i)}' +\n    'function say(t,bad){var m=$(\"msg\");m.textContent=t;m.className=bad?\"err\":\"\"}' +\n    'function post(p,b){return fetch(p,{method:\"POST\",headers:{\"Content-Type\":\"text/plain\"},body:JSON.stringify(b||{})}).then(function(r){return r.json()})}' +\n    'var busy=false;' +\n    'function show(d){$(\"s_setup\").textContent=d.setup===\"ready\"?\"ready\":d.setup===\"working\"?\"setting up…\":d.setup===\"nocobalt\"?\"Samsung YouTube not found\":d.setup===\"error\"?\"error: \"+d.error:\"not made yet\";' +\n    '$(\"s_script\").textContent=d.script===\"ready\"?\"TizenTube \"+d.scriptVersion:d.script===\"error\"?\"error: \"+d.scriptError:\"not downloaded yet\";' +\n    '$(\"s_proxy\").textContent=d.proxy===\"up\"?\"listening on \"+d.proxyAddress:d.proxyError?\"error: \"+d.proxyError:\"stopped\";' +\n    '$(\"s_pages\").textContent=d.pages?d.pages+(d.lastPage?\" (last \"+d.lastPage+\")\":\"\"):\"none yet\";' +\n    'if(!busy){$(\"tile\").checked=!!d.tileOn}' +\n    '$(\"tilenote\").textContent=d.tileState===\"on\"?\"On.\":d.tileState===\"waiting\"?\"Waiting: \"+d.tileNote:d.tileState===\"unsupported\"||d.tileState===\"error\"?d.tileNote:\"\"}' +\n    'function poll(){fetch(\"status\").then(function(r){return r.json()}).then(show).catch(function(){})}' +\n    '$(\"open\").onclick=function(){say(\"Preparing and starting… the first time takes up to a minute.\");post(\"open\").then(function(d){say(d.ok?(d.warning||\"YouTube is starting on the TV.\"):d.error,!d.ok||!!d.warning);poll()})};' +\n    '$(\"close\").onclick=function(){post(\"close\").then(function(){say(\"YouTube closed.\");poll()})};' +\n    '$(\"tile\").onchange=function(){busy=true;var on=$(\"tile\").checked;say(on?\"Preparing…\":\"Switching off…\");post(\"tile\",{on:on}).then(function(d){busy=false;say(d.ok?\"\":d.error,!d.ok);poll()},function(){busy=false})};' +\n    '$(\"clean\").onclick=function(){if(!confirm(\"Remove the certificate, the downloaded script and the copy of YouTube’s files?\"))return;post(\"cleanup\").then(function(d){say(d.ok?\"Removed.\":d.error,!d.ok);poll()})};' +\n    'poll();setInterval(poll,3000);' +\n    '</script></body>';\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var cfg = ctx.config.get();\n    var PORT = typeof cfg.port === 'number' && cfg.port % 1 === 0 && cfg.port >= 1024 && cfg.port < 65536 ? cfg.port : DEFAULT_PORT;\n    var script = new scriptLib.UserScript(setup.CACHE);\n    var logLines = [], preparing = null, alive = false, timer = null, watchTimer = null;\n    var tileOn = cfg.tile === true;\n    var lastSetup = 0, nextScriptTry = 0;\n    var st = { setup: 'idle', error: null, script: 'idle', scriptError: null, proxyError: null, pages: 0, lastPage: null, tileState: 'off', tileNote: '' };\n\n    function log(m) { logLines.push(new Date().toISOString().slice(11, 19) + ' ' + m); if (logLines.length > 150) logLines.shift(); }\n    function exec(shell, ms) { return ctx.execute(setup.wrap(shell), ms); }\n    function noop() {}\n\n    function saveConfig(patch) {\n        var c = ctx.config.get();\n        Object.keys(patch).forEach(function (k) { c[k] = patch[k]; });\n        try { ctx.config.set(c); } catch (e) { log('config not saved: ' + e.message); }\n    }\n\n    function readLeaf() {\n        try {\n            var key = fs.readFileSync(path.join(setup.DIR, 'leaf.key'));\n            var cert = fs.readFileSync(path.join(setup.DIR, 'leaf.crt'), 'utf8') + fs.readFileSync(path.join(setup.DIR, 'ca.crt'), 'utf8');\n            return { key: key, cert: cert };\n        } catch (e) { return null; }\n    }\n    function contentThere() { try { return fs.statSync(path.join(setup.CONTENT, 'ssl', 'certs')).isDirectory(); } catch (e) { return false; } }\n\n    var proxy = proxyLib.createProxy({\n        host: PROXY_HOST, port: PORT, log: log,\n        leaf: readLeaf,\n        script: function () { return script.load(); },\n        onPage: function () { st.pages++; st.lastPage = new Date().toISOString().slice(11, 19); }\n    });\n\n    function listen() {\n        return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {\n            proxy.listen(function (e) {\n                if (e) { st.proxyError = e.code === 'EADDRINUSE' ? 'port ' + PORT + ' is in use (put {\"port\": 8123} in config.json to change it)' : e.message; reject(new Error(st.proxyError)); }\n                else { st.proxyError = null; resolve(); }\n            });\n        });\n    }\n\n    function runSetup() {\n        st.setup = 'working'; st.error = null;\n        return exec(setup.setupScript(), 90000).then(function (r) {\n            var out = String((r && r.stdout) || '');\n            if (/^nocobalt$/m.test(out)) { st.setup = 'nocobalt'; throw new Error('Samsung’s YouTube app was not found on this TV'); }\n            if (!/^ready$/m.test(out)) { st.setup = 'error'; st.error = String((r && r.stderr) || out || 'setup failed').slice(0, 200); throw new Error(st.error); }\n            st.setup = 'ready'; lastSetup = Date.now();\n        }, function (e) { if (st.setup === 'working') { st.setup = 'error'; st.error = e.message; } throw e; });\n    }\n\n    function runScript() {\n        return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {\n            script.ensure(function (e) {\n                if (e) { st.script = 'error'; st.scriptError = e.message; nextScriptTry = Date.now() + SCRIPT_RETRY_MS; reject(e); }\n                else { st.script = 'ready'; st.scriptError = null; resolve(); }\n            });\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Certificate, script, proxy, in that order. The script is not essential: without it the proxy only tunnels and YouTube\n    // runs unpatched, so its failure is reported as a warning. Concurrent callers share one run.\n    // Resolves to {warning}; rejects when there is no certificate setup or no proxy.\n    function prepare() {\n        if (preparing) return preparing;\n        log('preparing');\n        var warning = null;\n        preparing = runSetup().then(function () { return runScript().catch(function (e) { warning = 'The script could not be downloaded (' + e.message + '): YouTube opens without the patches.'; }); })\n            .then(function () { return proxy.listening() ? null : listen(); })\n            .then(function () { preparing = null; log(warning ? 'ready, without the script' : 'ready'); return { warning: warning }; },\n                function (e) { preparing = null; log('prepare failed: ' + e.message); throw e; });\n        return preparing;\n    }\n\n    // Why the row may not be patched right now ('' when it may).\n    function blocker() {\n        if (!tileOn) return 'switched off';\n        if (!proxy.listening()) return st.proxyError ? st.proxyError : 'the proxy is not running';\n        if (!readLeaf() || !contentThere()) return 'the certificate is not ready';\n        if (!script.load()) return 'the script is not downloaded yet';\n        return '';\n    }\n\n    // Everything that changes the row goes through this queue, one job at a time, so a slow patch can never land after a restore.\n    var queue = Promise.resolve();\n    function serial(fn) { var r = queue.then(fn, fn); queue = r.then(noop, noop); return r; }\n\n    // Makes the row match what is wanted: patched when tile is on and everything is up, original otherwise. Idempotent.\n    // The decision is taken when the job runs, not when it is asked for; calls made while one is waiting share it.\n    var waiting = null, restoreTries = 0, retryTimer = null, bootTries = 0;\n    // The plugin starts before Vetro's root agent has connected (every boot), so the first jobs fail with \"no root agent\n    // connected\". Try again every few seconds instead of waiting for the next minute tick.\n    function retrySoon() {\n        if (!alive || retryTimer || bootTries++ >= 60) return;\n        retryTimer = setTimeout(function () { retryTimer = null; if (alive) reconcile(); }, 3000);\n        if (retryTimer.unref) retryTimer.unref();\n    }\n    function reconcile() {\n        if (waiting) return waiting;\n        waiting = serial(function () {\n            waiting = null;\n            var why = alive ? blocker() : 'the plugin is off';\n            var job = why ? tile.restore(exec) : tile.apply(exec, PROXY_HOST, PORT);\n            return job.then(function (state) {\n                if (why) {\n                    st.tileState = tileOn && alive ? 'waiting' : 'off'; st.tileNote = tileOn ? why : '';\n                    if (state === 'error' || state === 'raced' || state === 'patched' || state === 'stuck') {\n                        log('row restore: ' + state);\n                        // The flags are still there. Try again soon, a few times; the direct:// fallback keeps YouTube opening meanwhile.\n                        if (restoreTries++ < 5 && !retryTimer) {\n                            retryTimer = setTimeout(function () { retryTimer = null; reconcile(); }, 5000);\n                            if (retryTimer.unref) retryTimer.unref();\n                        }\n                    } else restoreTries = 0;\n                    return state;\n                }\n                restoreTries = 0;\n                if (state === 'patched') { if (st.tileState !== 'on') log('Samsung’s YouTube button now opens the patched app'); st.tileState = 'on'; st.tileNote = ''; }\n                else if (state === 'absent') { st.tileState = 'unsupported'; st.tileNote = 'This TV has no entry for Samsung’s YouTube app that can be changed.'; }\n                else if (state === 'foreign') { st.tileState = 'unsupported'; st.tileNote = 'Samsung’s YouTube settings are not in the expected form: left as they are.'; }\n                else { st.tileState = 'error'; st.tileNote = 'The TV’s app list could not be updated (' + state + '); trying again.'; log('row: ' + state); retrySoon(); }\n                if (st.tileState === 'on') bootTries = 0;\n                return state;\n            }, function (e) { st.tileState = 'error'; st.tileNote = 'Could not reach the TV’s app list: ' + e.message; log('row: ' + e.message); retrySoon(); return 'error'; });\n        });\n        return waiting;\n    }\n\n    // Once a minute while the button is on: keeps the proxy up, renews what expires, retries a failed download, and puts the row\n    // right again if Samsung rewrote it (an app update does).\n    function tick() {\n        if (!alive || !tileOn) return;\n        var chain = Promise.resolve();\n        if (Date.now() - lastSetup > SETUP_EVERY_MS && !preparing) chain = chain.then(function () { return runSetup().catch(function (e) { log('setup: ' + e.message); }); });\n        if (!script.load() && Date.now() > nextScriptTry && contentThere()) chain = chain.then(function () { return runScript().catch(noop); });\n        chain.then(function () { if (!proxy.listening() && readLeaf() && script.load()) return listen().catch(function (e) { log('proxy: ' + e.message); }); })\n            .then(function () { return reconcile(); }).catch(function (e) { log('tick: ' + e.message); });\n    }\n\n    // Samsung's YouTube started by the remote key, the Home tile or voice, without our flags (the TV's entry for it is missing after\n    // a boot, or Samsung rewrote it): close it and start it again through the proxy. At most 3 times in 2 minutes.\n    var watchBusy = false, relaunches = [], lastWhy = '', lastOut = null;\n    function watch() {\n        if (!alive || !tileOn || watchBusy) return;\n        var why = blocker();\n        if (why) { if (why !== lastWhy) log('watch idle: ' + why); lastWhy = why; return; }\n        lastWhy = '';\n        var now = Date.now();\n        relaunches = relaunches.filter(function (t) { return now - t < 120000; });\n        if (relaunches.length >= 3) return;\n        watchBusy = true;\n        exec(setup.checkScript(), 10000).then(function (r) {\n            var out = String((r && r.stdout) || '');\n            if (!/^relaunch$/m.test(out)) { if (out !== lastOut) log('watch: ' + (out.trim() || 'YouTube not running')); lastOut = out; return null; }\n            relaunches.push(Date.now());\n            log('YouTube was started without the patches: starting it again through the proxy');\n            return ctx.execute(setup.launchScript(PROXY_HOST, PORT), 25000);\n        }).then(function () { watchBusy = false; }, function (e) { watchBusy = false; log('watch: ' + e.message); });\n    }\n\n    function json(res, code, body) { res.writeHead(code, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'no-store' }); res.end(JSON.stringify(body)); }\n\n    function readJson(req, cb) {\n        var data = '', done = false;\n        function end(v) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(v); } }\n        req.on('data', function (c) { data += c; if (data.length > 2048) { req.destroy(); end({}); } });\n        req.on('end', function () { var v; try { v = JSON.parse(data || '{}'); } catch (e) { v = {}; } end(v && typeof v === 'object' ? v : {}); });\n        req.on('error', function () { end({}); });\n    }\n\n    function snapshot() {\n        var have = script.load(), s = proxy.stats();\n        return { setup: st.setup, error: st.error, script: have ? 'ready' : st.script, scriptVersion: scriptLib.VERSION, scriptError: st.scriptError,\n            proxy: proxy.listening() ? 'up' : 'down', proxyAddress: PROXY_HOST + ':' + PORT, proxyError: st.proxyError, pages: st.pages, lastPage: st.lastPage,\n            tileOn: tileOn, tileState: st.tileState, tileNote: st.tileNote, tunnels: s.tunnels, opened: s.opened, live: s.live };\n    }\n\n    return {\n        // Starts the proxy when a certificate and script from an earlier run are there (a YouTube that was left open keeps\n        // working after Vetro restarts), and brings the row in line: patched when the button is on, original otherwise.\n        // A first run does nothing until the page asks.\n        start: function () {\n            alive = true;\n            if (timer) clearInterval(timer);\n            timer = setInterval(function () { try { tick(); } catch (e) { log('tick: ' + e.message); } }, TICK_MS);\n            if (timer.unref) timer.unref();\n            if (watchTimer) clearInterval(watchTimer);\n            watchTimer = setInterval(function () { try { watch(); } catch (e) { log('watch: ' + e.message); } }, WATCH_MS);\n            if (watchTimer.unref) watchTimer.unref();\n            var ready = readLeaf() && script.load() ? listen().catch(function (e) { log('start: ' + e.message); }) : Promise.resolve();\n            ready.then(function () { return tileOn && !(readLeaf() && script.load() && contentThere()) ? prepare().catch(function (e) { log('start: ' + e.message); }) : null; })\n                .then(function () { return reconcile(); }).catch(function (e) { log('start: ' + e.message); });\n        },\n        // Puts the row back first: with the plugin off nothing is there to answer the proxy. A YouTube that is open keeps running\n        // (its proxy list falls back to a direct connection), so nothing is closed here.\n        stop: function () {\n            alive = false;\n            if (timer) { clearInterval(timer); timer = null; }\n            if (watchTimer) { clearInterval(watchTimer); watchTimer = null; }\n            // The proxy stays up until the row is back (a YouTube started in between still finds it), then stops listening.\n            // Resolves when that is done, so the fallback timer never outlives the stop.\n            return new Promise(function (resolve) {\n                var done = false, late = null;\n                var shut = function () {\n                    if (done) return;\n                    done = true;\n                    if (late) clearTimeout(late);\n                    if (!alive) proxy.close();\n                    resolve();\n                };\n                late = setTimeout(shut, 30000);\n                if (late.unref) late.unref();\n                reconcile().then(shut, shut);\n            });\n        },\n        status: function () { return { running: alive, proxy: proxy.listening(), setup: st.setup, script: script.load() ? scriptLib.VERSION : null, tile: st.tileState }; },\n\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n                res.end(PAGE);\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'status' && req.method === 'GET') { json(res, 200, snapshot()); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'log' && req.method === 'GET') { json(res, 200, { log: logLines }); return true; }\n            if (req.method !== 'POST') return false;\n            if (sub === 'open') {\n                var warning = null;\n                prepare().then(function (r) { warning = r.warning; return ctx.execute(setup.launchScript(PROXY_HOST, PORT), 25000); }).then(function (r) {\n                    var out = String((r && r.stdout) || '');\n                    if (!/successfully launched/.test(out)) throw new Error('YouTube did not start: ' + out.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').slice(0, 120));\n                    log('YouTube started');\n                    json(res, 200, warning ? { ok: true, warning: warning } : { ok: true });\n                }).catch(function (e) { json(res, 200, { ok: false, error: e.message }); });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'close') {\n                ctx.execute(setup.closeScript(), 15000).then(function () { json(res, 200, { ok: true }); }, function (e) { json(res, 200, { ok: false, error: e.message }); });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'tile') {\n                readJson(req, function (body) {\n                    if (typeof body.on !== 'boolean') { json(res, 200, { ok: false, error: 'Send {\"on\": true|false}' }); return; }\n                    tileOn = body.on;\n                    saveConfig({ tile: tileOn });\n                    var go = tileOn ? prepare().then(noop, function (e) { log('tile: ' + e.message); }) : Promise.resolve();\n                    go.then(function () { return reconcile(); }).then(function () { json(res, 200, { ok: true, state: st.tileState, note: st.tileNote }); },\n                        function (e) { json(res, 200, { ok: false, error: e.message }); });\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'cleanup') {\n                // The row first, in line with every other change to it: it points at files that are about to go.\n                tileOn = false; saveConfig({ tile: false });\n                serial(function () {\n                    return tile.restore(exec).then(function (state) {\n                        if (state !== 'original' && state !== 'absent' && state !== 'foreign') throw new Error('Samsung’s YouTube button could not be put back (' + state + '): nothing was removed');\n                        proxy.close(true); script.forget();\n                        return ctx.execute(setup.cleanupScript(), 30000);\n                    });\n                }).then(function () { st.setup = 'idle'; st.script = 'idle'; st.tileState = 'off'; st.tileNote = ''; lastSetup = 0; json(res, 200, { ok: true }); },\n                    function (e) { json(res, 200, { ok: false, error: e.message }); });\n                return true;\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n    };\n};\n","inject.js":"'use strict';\n// What changes in the YouTube TV page: a script tag before </body>, and a Content-Security-Policy that allows it.\n// Cobalt wants a CSP header on every page (without one it closes a few seconds after the page loads), so the original\n// is replaced, not just removed.\n\nvar SCRIPT_PATH = '/vetro-youtube/userscript.js';     // served by the proxy itself, on the youtube.com origin\n\nvar CSP = \"default-src * data: blob: 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval'; img-src * data: blob:; media-src * data: blob:; \" +\n    \"script-src * data: blob: 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval'; style-src * data: blob: 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src *; font-src * data:\";\n\nvar META_CSP_RE = /<meta\\b[^>]*http-equiv\\s*=\\s*[\"']Content-Security-Policy(?:-Report-Only)?[\"'][^>]*>/gi;\n\n// The TV app's start page: /tv or /tv?..., not /tv_config or anything else that merely starts with /tv.\nfunction isTvPage(url) { return url === '/tv' || url.indexOf('/tv?') === 0 || url.indexOf('/tv#') === 0; }\n\nfunction scriptTag(version) { return '<script src=\"' + SCRIPT_PATH + '?v=' + encodeURIComponent(version) + '\"></script>'; }\n\n// -> {html, injected}. Without a </body> the tag goes at the end of the document.\nfunction rewritePage(html, tag) {\n    var text = String(html).replace(META_CSP_RE, '');\n    var at = text.indexOf('</body>');\n    if (at < 0) return { html: text + tag, injected: false };\n    return { html: text.slice(0, at) + tag + text.slice(at), injected: true };\n}\n\n// Response headers of the rewritten page: no CSP from YouTube, ours instead; length and encoding are recomputed.\nfunction pageHeaders(upstream, byteLength) {\n    var h = {};\n    Object.keys(upstream).forEach(function (k) {\n        if (k === 'content-security-policy' || k === 'content-security-policy-report-only' || k === 'content-length' ||\n            k === 'content-encoding' || k === 'alt-svc') return;\n        h[k] = upstream[k];\n    });\n    h['content-security-policy'] = CSP;\n    h['content-length'] = byteLength;\n    return h;\n}\n\n// Headers of everything else: unchanged, except an alt-svc that would send the app to YouTube over QUIC, around the proxy.\nfunction passHeaders(upstream) {\n    var h = {};\n    Object.keys(upstream).forEach(function (k) { if (k !== 'alt-svc') h[k] = upstream[k]; });\n    return h;\n}\n\n// Only these hosts are opened up and rewritten; every other host is a plain tunnel.\nvar MITM_HOSTS = { 'www.youtube.com': 1, 'youtube.com': 1 };\n\nmodule.exports = { SCRIPT_PATH: SCRIPT_PATH, CSP: CSP, isTvPage: isTvPage, scriptTag: scriptTag, rewritePage: rewritePage,\n    pageHeaders: pageHeaders, passHeaders: passHeaders, MITM_HOSTS: MITM_HOSTS };\n","proxy.js":"'use strict';\n// The proxy YouTube is started with (--proxy). Everything is a plain tunnel except www.youtube.com, which is opened with\n// the plugin's own certificate (trusted only by the YouTube app this plugin starts) so the /tv page can get its script.\n// Without a certificate or without the script it only tunnels: YouTube then runs unpatched instead of breaking.\n// Listens on 127.0.0.2 (Chromium sends 127.0.0.1 around a proxy).\n//\n// This code runs inside Vetro's process, so nothing may throw out of an event handler: every callback goes through guard(),\n// every socket has an error listener, every connection has a timeout, and the number of connections is capped.\n\nvar net = require('net');\nvar tls = require('tls');\nvar http = require('http');\nvar client = require('./tls-client.js');\nvar inject = require('./inject.js');\n\nvar MAX_BODY = 8 * 1024 * 1024;\nvar MAX_CONNECTIONS = 300;\nvar IDLE_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000;           // a connection that carries nothing for this long is closed\nvar CONNECT_MS = 20 * 1000;            // time allowed to reach a host\n\n// opts: host, port, log(msg), leaf() -> {key, cert} | null, script() -> {body, version} | null, onPage({injected, bytes}), maxConnections\nfunction createProxy(opts) {\n    var server = null, ready = false, tlsServer = null, httpServer = null, leafCert = null, tunnels = 0, opened = 0, live = 0, refused = 0;\n    var socks = {}, nextId = 1, waiters = [];                // every open socket, so that close(true) can end them\n    var cap = opts.maxConnections || MAX_CONNECTIONS;\n\n    function guard(fn, onError) {\n        return function () {\n            try { return fn.apply(this, arguments); }\n            catch (e) { try { opts.log('internal error: ' + (e && e.message)); if (onError) onError(e); } catch (x) { /* nothing more to do */ } }\n        };\n    }\n    function drop(sock) { try { sock.destroy(); } catch (e) { /* closed */ } }\n    function track(sock) {\n        live++;\n        var gone = false, id = nextId++;\n        socks[id] = sock;\n        sock.on('close', function () { if (!gone) { gone = true; live--; delete socks[id]; } });\n        sock.on('error', function () { /* the close that follows is handled */ });\n        sock.setTimeout(IDLE_MS, function () { drop(sock); });\n    }\n\n    function handle(req, res) {\n        var abortUpstream = null;\n        res.on('error', function () { /* the app went away */ });\n        req.on('error', function () { if (abortUpstream) abortUpstream(); });\n        res.on('close', function () { if (abortUpstream) abortUpstream(); });\n        var fail = function () { try { if (!res.headersSent) res.writeHead(502, { 'content-length': 0 }); res.end(); } catch (e) { drop(res.socket || req.socket); } };\n\n        var host = String(req.headers.host || '').replace(/:\\d+$/, '').toLowerCase();\n        if (!inject.MITM_HOSTS[host]) { res.writeHead(421, { 'content-length': 0 }); res.end(); return; }\n        if (req.url.split('?')[0] === inject.SCRIPT_PATH) {\n            var s = opts.script();\n            if (req.method !== 'GET' || !s) { res.writeHead(404, { 'content-length': 0 }); res.end(); return; }\n            res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'application/javascript; charset=utf-8', 'content-length': s.body.length, 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n            res.end(s.body);\n            return;\n        }\n        var tv = req.method === 'GET' && inject.isTvPage(req.url) && !!opts.script();\n        var chunks = [], size = 0, over = false;\n        req.on('data', function (c) { size += c.length; if (size > MAX_BODY) { over = true; return; } chunks.push(c); });\n        req.on('end', guard(function () {\n            if (over) { res.writeHead(413, { 'content-length': 0 }); res.end(); return; }\n            var h = client.request({ host: host, method: req.method, path: req.url, headers: req.headers, identity: tv }, Buffer.concat(chunks), guard(function (err, r) {\n                if (err) { opts.log('upstream ' + host + ' failed: ' + err.message); fail(); return; }\n                var type = String(r.headers['content-type'] || '');\n                if (!tv || r.status !== 200 || type.indexOf('text/html') < 0) {\n                    res.writeHead(r.status, inject.passHeaders(r.headers));\n                    r.body.on('error', function () { drop(res.socket); });\n                    r.body.pipe(res);\n                    return;\n                }\n                var parts = [], total = 0;\n                r.body.on('data', function (c) { total += c.length; if (total <= MAX_BODY) parts.push(c); });\n                r.body.on('error', function () { fail(); });\n                r.body.on('end', guard(function () {\n                    if (total > MAX_BODY) { fail(); return; }\n                    var s2 = opts.script();\n                    var page = inject.rewritePage(Buffer.concat(parts).toString('utf8'), inject.scriptTag(s2 ? s2.version : '0'));\n                    var out = Buffer.from ? Buffer.from(page.html, 'utf8') : new Buffer(page.html, 'utf8');\n                    res.writeHead(200, inject.pageHeaders(r.headers, out.length));\n                    res.end(out);\n                    opts.log('TV page rewritten (' + out.length + ' bytes' + (page.injected ? '' : ', no </body>: tag appended') + ')');\n                    if (opts.onPage) opts.onPage({ injected: true, bytes: out.length });\n                }, fail));\n            }, fail));\n            abortUpstream = function () { h.abort(); };\n        }, fail));\n    }\n\n    // One shared TLS and HTTP server for every opened connection; rebuilt when the certificate changes.\n    function ensureTls() {\n        var leaf = opts.leaf();\n        if (!leaf) return null;\n        if (tlsServer && leafCert === leaf.cert) return tlsServer;\n        httpServer = http.createServer(guard(handle, null));\n        httpServer.on('clientError', function (e, sock) { opts.log('client error: ' + (e && e.code || e)); drop(sock); });\n        tlsServer = tls.createServer({ key: leaf.key, cert: leaf.cert });\n        tlsServer.on('secureConnection', guard(function (s) { track(s); httpServer.emit('connection', s); }));\n        tlsServer.on('tlsClientError', function (e) { opts.log('TLS refused by the app: ' + (e && e.message)); });\n        tlsServer.on('error', function () { /* per connection errors are on the sockets */ });\n        leafCert = leaf.cert;\n        return tlsServer;\n    }\n\n    var HEAD_MAX = 8192;\n\n    function onConnection(c) {\n        if (live >= cap) { refused++; drop(c); return; }\n        track(c);\n        var buf = Buffer.alloc ? Buffer.alloc(0) : new Buffer(0), started = false;\n        c.on('data', guard(function onData(d) {\n            if (started) return;\n            buf = Buffer.concat([buf, d]);\n            var end = buf.indexOf('\\r\\n\\r\\n');\n            if (end < 0) {\n                if (buf.length > HEAD_MAX) { started = true; c.end('HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\\r\\nconnection: close\\r\\ncontent-length: 0\\r\\n\\r\\n'); }\n                return;                                    // the rest of the request has not arrived yet\n            }\n            started = true;\n            c.removeListener('data', onData);\n            c.pause();\n            var rest = buf.slice(end + 4);\n            connect(c, buf.slice(0, end).toString('binary').split('\\r\\n')[0], rest);\n        }));\n    }\n\n    function connect(c, line, rest) {\n        var m = /^CONNECT ([^ :\\[\\]]+):(\\d{1,5}) HTTP\\/1\\.[01]$/.exec(line);\n        if (!m) { c.end('HTTP/1.1 502 Bad Gateway\\r\\nconnection: close\\r\\ncontent-length: 0\\r\\n\\r\\n'); return; }\n        var host = m[1].toLowerCase(), port = parseInt(m[2], 10);\n        if (port < 1 || port > 65535) { c.end('HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\\r\\nconnection: close\\r\\ncontent-length: 0\\r\\n\\r\\n'); return; }\n        if (port === 443 && inject.MITM_HOSTS[host] && opts.script() && !rest.length) {\n            var t = ensureTls();\n            if (t) {\n                opened++;\n                c.write('HTTP/1.1 200 Connection Established\\r\\n\\r\\n');\n                t.emit('connection', c);\n                c.resume();\n                return;\n            }\n        }\n        tunnels++;\n        var up = net.connect(port, host);\n        track(up);\n        up.setTimeout(CONNECT_MS, guard(function () { if (!up.connecting) return; drop(up); drop(c); }));\n        up.on('connect', guard(function () {\n            up.setTimeout(IDLE_MS, function () { drop(up); });\n            c.write('HTTP/1.1 200 Connection Established\\r\\n\\r\\n');\n            if (rest.length) up.write(rest);\n            c.pipe(up); up.pipe(c);\n            c.resume();\n        }));\n        up.on('error', function () { drop(c); });\n        c.on('close', function () { drop(up); });\n        up.on('close', function () { drop(c); });\n    }\n\n    return {\n        listen: function (cb) {\n            if (server) { if (ready) cb(null); else waiters.push(cb); return; }\n            var s = net.createServer(guard(onConnection)), done = false;\n            server = s; ready = false;\n            s.on('error', function (e) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(e); waiters.splice(0).forEach(function (w) { w(e); }); } else opts.log('proxy error: ' + e.message); if (server === s) { server = null; ready = false; } });\n            s.on('close', function () { if (server === s) { server = null; ready = false; } });\n            s.listen(opts.port, opts.host, function () { if (!done && server === s) { done = true; ready = true; cb(null); waiters.splice(0).forEach(function (w) { w(null); }); } else if (!done) { done = true; try { s.close(); } catch (e) { /* closed */ } var err = new Error('closed while starting'); cb(err); waiters.splice(0).forEach(function (w) { w(err); }); } });\n        },\n        // Stops listening. Connections that are already open are left to finish on their own (a YouTube that is running keeps\n        // working), unless `hard` is set: then they are cut as well.\n        close: function (hard) {\n            var s = server;\n            server = null; ready = false;\n            if (s) { try { s.close(); } catch (e) { /* closed */ } }\n            tlsServer = null; httpServer = null; leafCert = null;\n            if (hard) Object.keys(socks).forEach(function (id) { drop(socks[id]); });\n        },\n        listening: function () { return !!server && ready; },\n        stats: function () { return { tunnels: tunnels, opened: opened, live: live, refused: refused }; }\n    };\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { createProxy: createProxy, MAX_CONNECTIONS: MAX_CONNECTIONS };\n","setup.js":"'use strict';\n// Shell pieces run as root through ctx.execute: the certificate setup, starting and closing the YouTube app, and cleanup.\n// Everything the plugin keeps outside its own folder is under DIR.\n\nvar DIR = '/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vetro-youtube';\nvar CACHE = DIR + '/cache';\n// The copy of the YouTube app's content folder. Its path is kept very short on purpose: Samsung's own tile passes the app at most\n// 127 characters of flags, and Samsung's flags already take about 50 of them.\nvar CONTENT = '/opt/usr/home/owner/share/vyt';\nvar COBALT = '/usr/apps/com.samsung.tv.cobalt/content/app/cobalt';\nvar APP = 'com.samsung.tv.cobalt-yt';       // Samsung's YouTube\nvar USER = 5001;\n\nfunction toBase64(text) { return (Buffer.from && Buffer.from !== Uint8Array.from ? Buffer.from(text) : new Buffer(text)).toString('base64'); }\nfunction wrap(script) { return 'echo ' + toBase64(script) + ' | base64 -d | sh'; }\n\n// Makes (once, and again when something expires or Samsung's YouTube changed) three things in DIR:\n//  - a certificate authority of its own (ca.key stays root-only) and a certificate for youtube.com signed by it (leaf.*);\n//  - CONTENT, a copy of the YouTube app's content folder with that authority added to its trust store. The app is started with\n//    --content pointing here, so the authority is trusted by that app alone, never by the TV.\n// Prints one word: ready | nocobalt.\nfunction setupScript() {\n    return [\n        'set -e',\n        'umask 022',\n        \"D='\" + DIR + \"'\",\n        \"C='\" + CONTENT + \"'\",\n        \"SRC='\" + COBALT + \"/content'\",\n        \"LIB='\" + COBALT + \"/lib/libcobalt.so'\",\n        '[ -d \"$SRC/ssl/certs\" ] || { echo nocobalt; exit 0; }',\n        // DIR belongs to root: the user the TV apps run as cannot swap a file for a link that a root command below would follow.\n        // Only cache/ is theirs (the downloaded script, verified by hash on every read).\n        'mkdir -p \"$D\"; chown root:root \"$D\"; chmod 755 \"$D\"; cd \"$D\"',\n        'for f in ca.key ca.crt ca.cnf ca.srl leaf.key leaf.crt leaf.csr leaf.ext content.stamp cache \"$C\"; do [ -L \"$f\" ] && rm -f \"$f\"; done',\n        'if [ -f ca.key ] && [ ! -O ca.key ]; then rm -rf ca.key ca.crt leaf.key leaf.crt leaf.csr ca.srl \"$C\" content.stamp; fi',\n        'rm -rf content',                                     // where the copy used to be (before the path had to be short)\n        '[ -d cache ] || mkdir cache; chown owner:users cache; chmod 755 cache',\n        'if [ ! -f ca.key ] || [ ! -f ca.crt ] || ! openssl x509 -in ca.crt -noout -checkend 2592000 >/dev/null 2>&1; then',\n        '  rm -rf ca.key ca.crt leaf.key leaf.crt leaf.csr ca.srl \"$C\" content.stamp',\n        \"  printf '%s\\\\n' '[req]' 'distinguished_name=dn' 'x509_extensions=v3' 'prompt=no' '[dn]' 'CN=Vetro YouTube Local CA' '[v3]' 'basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE' 'keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign' 'subjectKeyIdentifier=hash' > ca.cnf\",\n        '  openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -keyout ca.key -out ca.crt -days 3650 -sha256 -config ca.cnf >/dev/null 2>&1',\n        'fi',\n        'STAMP=\"v3-$(stat -c %Y \"$LIB\" 2>/dev/null)-$(openssl x509 -in ca.crt -noout -fingerprint -sha256)\"',\n        'if [ ! -d \"$C\" ] || [ ! -O \"$C\" ] || [ \"$(cat content.stamp 2>/dev/null)\" != \"$STAMP\" ]; then',\n        '  rm -rf \"$C\" content.stamp; cp -R \"$SRC\" \"$C\"',\n        '  cp ca.crt \"$C/ssl/certs/$(openssl x509 -in ca.crt -noout -subject_hash).0\"',\n        '  cp ca.crt \"$C/ssl/certs/$(openssl x509 -in ca.crt -noout -subject_hash_old).0\"',\n        '  echo \"$STAMP\" > content.stamp',\n        'fi',\n        'if [ ! -f leaf.crt ] || [ ! -f leaf.key ] || ! openssl x509 -in leaf.crt -noout -checkend 2592000 >/dev/null 2>&1 || ! openssl verify -CAfile ca.crt leaf.crt >/dev/null 2>&1; then',\n        '  openssl req -new -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -keyout leaf.key -subj /CN=www.youtube.com -out leaf.csr >/dev/null 2>&1',\n        \"  printf '%s\\\\n' 'subjectAltName=DNS:www.youtube.com,DNS:youtube.com' 'basicConstraints=CA:FALSE' 'keyUsage=digitalSignature,keyEncipherment' 'extendedKeyUsage=serverAuth' > leaf.ext\",\n        '  openssl x509 -req -in leaf.csr -CA ca.crt -CAkey ca.key -CAcreateserial -out leaf.crt -days 397 -sha256 -extfile leaf.ext >/dev/null 2>&1',\n        'fi',\n        'chown root:root ca.key; chown owner:users leaf.key leaf.crt ca.crt; chmod 600 ca.key leaf.key; chmod 644 ca.crt leaf.crt',\n        'echo ready'\n    ].join('\\n');\n}\n\n// What Samsung's own tile passes to the YouTube app (metadata native.userdata of 9Ur5IzDKqV.TizenYouTube), plus the proxy and\n// the content folder. The proxy list ends in direct://: if the proxy is down the app connects directly (unpatched) instead of\n// showing a network error. The value of USERDATA starts with a space on purpose: without it app_launcher reads the value as one\n// of its own options.\nvar SAMSUNG_ARGS = '--base_url=https://www.youtube.com/tv --dial_name=YouTube --use_eden --start_frag=#start';\n\n// No http:// in front of the proxy address (it is the default) and a short content path: see CONTENT.\nfunction proxyArgs(proxyHost, proxyPort) { return '--proxy=' + proxyHost + ':' + proxyPort + ',direct:// --content=' + CONTENT; }\n\nfunction launchScript(proxyHost, proxyPort) {\n    var args = ' ' + SAMSUNG_ARGS + ' ' + proxyArgs(proxyHost, proxyPort);\n    return 'app_launcher -t ' + APP + ' -u ' + USER + ' >/dev/null 2>&1; sleep 1; app_launcher -s ' + APP + ' -u ' + USER + \" USERDATA '\" + args + \"' 2>&1\";\n}\n\n// Prints \"relaunch\" when Samsung's YouTube is running without our proxy flags (started by the remote key or a voice command\n// while the TV's own entry for it is missing or not patched yet, which is the case after every boot), \"ok\" when it is\n// running patched, and nothing when it is not running. The app's command line carries its flags as one base64 text.\nfunction checkScript() {\n    return [\n        'R=',\n        'for p in $(pgrep -f \"^/usr/apps/com.samsung.tv.cobalt/bin/cobalt_launcher\"); do',\n        '  D=$(tr \"\\\\0\" \"\\\\n\" < /proc/$p/cmdline | sed -n 4p | base64 -d 2>/dev/null | tr -c \"[:print:]\" \" \")',\n        '  case \"$D\" in *dial_name=YouTube*) case \"$D\" in *share/vyt*) R=ok;; *) R=relaunch; break;; esac;; esac',\n        'done',\n        'echo $R'\n    ].join('\\n');\n}\n\nfunction closeScript() { return 'app_launcher -t ' + APP + ' -u ' + USER + ' 2>&1'; }\n\n// Everything this plugin put on the TV outside its own folder.\nfunction cleanupScript() { return closeScript() + '; rm -rf \"' + DIR + '\" \"' + CONTENT + '\"; echo removed'; }\n\nmodule.exports = { DIR: DIR, CACHE: CACHE, CONTENT: CONTENT, APP: APP, SAMSUNG_ARGS: SAMSUNG_ARGS, proxyArgs: proxyArgs, wrap: wrap, setupScript: setupScript, launchScript: launchScript, checkScript: checkScript, closeScript: closeScript, cleanupScript: cleanupScript };\n","tile.js":"'use strict';\n// Makes Samsung's YouTube button (Home tile, remote key, voice, casting) open the patched app.\n//\n// All of them start the wrapper app 9Ur5IzDKqV.TizenYouTube, which starts the YouTube app with the flags kept in one row of the\n// web app service's database (/opt/dbspace/.webappservice.db, table widgetinfo, column reserved_string_6; the same text is also\n// in the app's config.xml and in the package database, but neither is read when the app starts - checked on a Q80A, fw 2310.0).\n// This module appends the proxy and content flags to that column and takes them off again. The change is a suffix, so undoing it needs no saved copy: it cuts the suffix off.\n//\n// Safety rules, in order of importance:\n//  - The proxy list ends in direct://: with the proxy down YouTube still opens, just unpatched.\n//  - A write is a compare-and-swap (it only happens if the row still holds the value that was read), so a change made by\n//    Samsung or by someone else in between is never overwritten.\n//  - Only that one row of that one app is touched, and only when it holds a plain printable value without quotes.\n//  - Whoever calls apply() decides when the row may be patched (proxy listening, certificate and script ready); this module\n//    only knows how.\n\nvar setup = require('./setup.js');\n\nvar DB = '/opt/dbspace/.webappservice.db';\nvar WRAPPER = '9Ur5IzDKqV.TizenYouTube';      // the row's tizen_id\nvar COLUMN = 'reserved_string_6';\nvar ORIGINAL_START = '--base_url=https://www.youtube.com/tv';      // what Samsung's value starts with: anything else is not ours to edit\n// The most characters the TV passes on to the YouTube app from this value (checked on a Q80A: it cuts at 127, silently, so a longer\n// value loses its last flags and the app starts without --content, and without trusting the plugin's certificate).\nvar MAX_VALUE = 127;\n\n// Samsung's own value already has ORIGINAL_START, which is also what the app does without it (its default address), so there is no\n// room for both that and our flags. Patching takes ORIGINAL_START out and appends ours; un-patching takes ours out and puts\n// ORIGINAL_START back in front. Nothing is saved: the one string that is removed is a constant.\n\n// Our two flags wherever they sit in the value (a firmware that appends its own flag after them must not hide them).\nvar OURS = '--content=' + setup.CONTENT;\nvar SUFFIX_RE = new RegExp(' --proxy=[0-9.]+:\\\\d{1,5},direct:// --content=' + setup.CONTENT.replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_]/g, '\\\\$&') + '(?= |$)', 'g');\n\n// Printable ASCII only, and none of the characters a shell or SQL string could be broken with.\nfunction plain(v) { return typeof v === 'string' && v.length > 0 && v.length < 600 && /^[\\x20-\\x7e]+$/.test(v) && !/['\"\\\\$`]/.test(v); }\n\nfunction isPatched(value) { SUFFIX_RE.lastIndex = 0; return SUFFIX_RE.test(String(value)); }\n\n// Does the text still carry our flags (even in a form this module will not edit)?\nfunction hasOurs(value) { return String(value).indexOf(OURS) >= 0; }\n\n// The value without our flags and with ORIGINAL_START back in front (a value that is not patched comes back unchanged).\nfunction original(value) {\n    var v = String(value);\n    if (!isPatched(v)) return v;\n    v = v.replace(SUFFIX_RE, '').replace(/^ +/, '');\n    return v.indexOf(ORIGINAL_START) === 0 ? v : ORIGINAL_START + (v ? ' ' + v : '');\n}\n\n// The value that starts the app through the proxy: Samsung's flags without ORIGINAL_START, then ours (an older suffix is\n// replaced, never doubled). Returns null when it would not fit.\nfunction patched(value, proxyHost, proxyPort) {\n    var rest = original(value);\n    if (rest.indexOf(ORIGINAL_START) === 0) rest = rest.slice(ORIGINAL_START.length).replace(/^ +/, '');\n    var out = (rest ? rest + ' ' : '') + setup.proxyArgs(proxyHost, proxyPort);\n    return out.length <= MAX_VALUE ? out : null;\n}\n\nvar WHERE = \"tizen_id='\" + WRAPPER + \"'\";\n\n// Prints the value, or nothing; one line per row (more than one row is reported by the caller as unexpected).\nfunction readScript(db) {\n    var d = db || DB;\n    return '[ -f \"' + d + '\" ] || { echo \"Error: no package database\"; exit 0; }\\n' +\n        'sqlite3 -cmd \".timeout 8000\" \"' + d + '\" \"select ' + COLUMN + ' from widgetinfo where ' + WHERE + ';\" 2>&1';\n}\n\n// Compare-and-swap. Prints swapped | changed (the row no longer held `from`) | failed.\nfunction swapScript(from, to, db) {\n    if (!plain(from) || !plain(to)) throw new Error('refusing to write a value that is not plain printable text');\n    var d = db || DB;\n    return [\n        'DB=\"' + d + '\"',\n        '[ -f \"$DB\" ] || { echo failed; exit 0; }',\n        'OWN=$(stat -c %u:%g \"$DB\" 2>/dev/null)',\n        'N=$(sqlite3 -cmd \".timeout 8000\" \"$DB\" \"update widgetinfo set ' + COLUMN + \"='\" + to + \"' where \" + WHERE + ' and ' + COLUMN + \"='\" + from + \"'; select changes();\\\" 2>/dev/null) || { echo failed; exit 0; }\",\n        'if [ \"$N\" = \"1\" ]; then',\n        '  [ -n \"$OWN\" ] && chown \"$OWN\" \"$DB\" \"$DB-journal\" 2>/dev/null; echo swapped',\n        'else echo changed; fi'\n    ].join('\\n');\n}\n\n// state: 'original' | 'patched' | 'absent' (no such row: another firmware) | 'foreign' (a value this module will not edit, without our flags)\n// | 'stuck' (our flags are in a value this module will not edit) | 'error'\nfunction classify(output) {\n    var text = String(output || '').replace(/\\r/g, '');\n    var lines = text.split('\\n').filter(function (l) { return l.length; });\n    if (!lines.length) return { state: 'absent', value: null };\n    if (lines.length > 1 || /^(Error|sqlite3:|Parse error)/i.test(lines[0]) || /database is locked/i.test(text)) return { state: 'error', value: null, detail: lines[0].slice(0, 120) };\n    var v = lines[0];\n    if (!plain(v)) return hasOurs(v) ? { state: 'stuck', value: null } : { state: 'foreign', value: null };\n    if (isPatched(v)) return { state: 'patched', value: v, valid: v.indexOf(ORIGINAL_START) === 0 || v.indexOf('--base_url=') < 0 };\n    if (hasOurs(v)) return { state: 'stuck', value: null };\n    return v.indexOf(ORIGINAL_START) === 0 ? { state: 'original', value: v } : { state: 'foreign', value: null };\n}\n\n// execute(shellText, timeoutMs) -> Promise<{stdout}>, already wrapped for the TV by the caller.\nfunction read(execute, db) {\n    return execute(readScript(db), 15000).then(function (r) { return classify(r && r.stdout); });\n}\n\nfunction swap(execute, from, to, db) {\n    return execute(swapScript(from, to, db), 20000).then(function (r) {\n        var out = String((r && r.stdout) || '');\n        return /^swapped$/m.test(out) ? 'swapped' : /^changed$/m.test(out) ? 'changed' : 'failed';\n    });\n}\n\n// Makes the row hold the patched value for this proxy. Resolves to the state afterwards: 'patched' | 'absent' | 'foreign' | 'stuck' | 'error' | 'raced'.\nfunction apply(execute, proxyHost, proxyPort, db) {\n    return read(execute, db).then(function (cur) {\n        if (cur.state !== 'original' && cur.state !== 'patched') return cur.state;\n        if (cur.valid === false) return 'foreign';\n        var want = patched(cur.value, proxyHost, proxyPort);\n        if (want === null) return 'foreign';                        // would not fit in what the TV passes on\n        if (want === cur.value) return 'patched';\n        return swap(execute, cur.value, want, db).then(function (r) { return r === 'swapped' ? 'patched' : r === 'changed' ? 'raced' : 'error'; });\n    });\n}\n\n// Takes the suffix off. Resolves to 'original' | 'absent' | 'foreign' | 'stuck' | 'error' | 'raced'. Only 'original', 'absent' and 'foreign' mean no flag of ours is left.\nfunction restore(execute, db) {\n    return read(execute, db).then(function (cur) {\n        if (cur.state === 'original') return 'original';\n        if (cur.state !== 'patched') return cur.state;\n        return swap(execute, cur.value, original(cur.value), db).then(function (r) { return r === 'swapped' ? 'original' : r === 'changed' ? 'raced' : 'error'; });\n    });\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { MAX_VALUE: MAX_VALUE, hasOurs: hasOurs, DB: DB, WRAPPER: WRAPPER, COLUMN: COLUMN, plain: plain, isPatched: isPatched, original: original, patched: patched,\n    readScript: readScript, swapScript: swapScript, classify: classify, read: read, apply: apply, restore: restore };\n","tls-client.js":"'use strict';\n// A small HTTPS client for the proxy. Node 12.4 on the TV cannot raise its HTTP header limit (the option arrived in\n// 12.17), and YouTube's response headers are bigger than the default 8 KB, so http.request fails with\n// HPE_HEADER_OVERFLOW. This one reads the response head by hand. Plain ES5.\n\nvar tls = require('tls');\nvar PassThrough = require('stream').PassThrough;\n\nfunction bytes(n) { return Buffer.alloc ? Buffer.alloc(n) : new Buffer(n); }\n\n// Turns a chunked body into plain bytes written to `out`. Feed it with write(buffer).\nfunction Dechunk(out) {\n    var buf = bytes(0), state = 'size', left = 0;\n    this.complete = function () { return state === 'done'; };\n    this.write = function (d) {\n        buf = Buffer.concat([buf, d]);\n        for (;;) {\n            if (state === 'size') {\n                var i = buf.indexOf('\\r\\n');\n                if (i < 0) return;\n                left = parseInt(buf.slice(0, i).toString('binary'), 16);\n                buf = buf.slice(i + 2);\n                if (left !== left || left < 0) { state = 'bad'; if (out.abort) out.abort(new Error('bad chunk size')); return; }\n                if (left === 0) { state = 'done'; if (!out.destroyed && out.writable) out.end(); return; }\n                state = 'data';\n            } else if (state === 'data') {\n                if (!buf.length) return;\n                var n = Math.min(left, buf.length);\n                if (!out.destroyed && out.writable) out.write(buf.slice(0, n));\n                buf = buf.slice(n);\n                left -= n;\n                if (left === 0) state = 'crlf';\n            } else if (state === 'crlf') {\n                if (buf.length < 2) return;\n                buf = buf.slice(2);\n                state = 'size';\n            } else return;\n        }\n    };\n}\n\n// Headers that describe one hop, not the message: never forwarded in either direction.\nvar HOP = { 'connection': 1, 'proxy-connection': 1, 'keep-alive': 1, 'te': 1, 'upgrade': 1, 'transfer-encoding': 1,\n    'content-length': 1, 'proxy-authorization': 1, 'proxy-authenticate': 1, 'trailer': 1 };\n\n// Header names listed in a Connection header describe this hop only.\nfunction nominated(value) {\n    var out = {};\n    String(value || '').split(',').forEach(function (t) { t = t.trim().toLowerCase(); if (t) out[t] = 1; });\n    return out;\n}\n\n// \"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\\r\\nA: b\" -> {status, headers, chunked, length}. Header names are lower case, repeated ones become arrays.\n// A chunked body is reported with chunked:true and without its transfer-encoding and content-length headers. `length` is the\n// declared body length, or -1 when there is none to rely on.\nfunction parseHead(text) {\n    var lines = text.split('\\r\\n'), m = /^HTTP\\/1\\.[01] (\\d{3})/.exec(lines[0]);\n    var out = { status: m ? parseInt(m[1], 10) : 0, headers: {}, chunked: false, length: -1 }, hop = {};\n    for (var i = 1; i < lines.length; i++) {\n        var j = lines[i].indexOf(':');\n        if (j < 1) continue;\n        var k = lines[i].slice(0, j).toLowerCase(), v = lines[i].slice(j + 1).replace(/^\\s+/, '');\n        if (k === 'transfer-encoding') { if (/chunked/i.test(v)) out.chunked = true; continue; }\n        if (k === 'connection') { var n = nominated(v); Object.keys(n).forEach(function (t) { hop[t] = 1; }); continue; }\n        if (k === 'keep-alive' || k === 'proxy-connection') continue;\n        if (out.headers[k] === undefined) out.headers[k] = v;\n        else if (Array.isArray(out.headers[k])) out.headers[k].push(v);\n        else out.headers[k] = [out.headers[k], v];\n    }\n    Object.keys(hop).forEach(function (t) { delete out.headers[t]; });\n    var cl = out.headers['content-length'];\n    if (cl !== undefined) {\n        var vals = Array.isArray(cl) ? cl : [cl], ok = vals.every(function (x) { return /^\\d{1,15}$/.test(x) && x === vals[0]; });\n        if (ok && !out.chunked) out.length = parseInt(vals[0], 10);\n        if (out.chunked || !ok) delete out.headers['content-length'];\n    }\n    return out;\n}\n\n// The request head as bytes. `headers` is a Node-style object (lower case names). The body length is always declared.\nfunction buildRequest(opts, bodyLength) {\n    var lines = [opts.method + ' ' + opts.path + ' HTTP/1.1'], hop = {};\n    Object.keys(opts.headers || {}).forEach(function (k) { if (k.toLowerCase() === 'connection') { var v = opts.headers[k]; hop = nominated(Array.isArray(v) ? v.join(',') : v); } });\n    Object.keys(opts.headers || {}).forEach(function (k) {\n        var key = k.toLowerCase();\n        if (HOP[key] || hop[key]) return;\n        if (key === 'accept-encoding' && opts.identity) return;\n        var v = opts.headers[k];\n        (Array.isArray(v) ? v : [v]).forEach(function (x) {\n            if (/[\\r\\n]/.test(String(x))) return;           // never let a value start a second header\n            lines.push(key + ': ' + x);\n        });\n    });\n    if (opts.identity) lines.push('accept-encoding: identity');\n    if (bodyLength || (opts.method !== 'GET' && opts.method !== 'HEAD')) lines.push('content-length: ' + bodyLength);\n    lines.push('connection: close');\n    return lines.join('\\r\\n') + '\\r\\n\\r\\n';\n}\n\n// request({host, port, method, path, headers, identity, timeout}, bodyBuffer, cb)\n// cb(err) once, or cb(null, {status, headers, body}) where body is a readable stream of the decoded payload.\n// The stream ends normally only when the whole body arrived (declared length reached, last chunk seen, or a close for a body\n// with neither); anything shorter ends with an 'error' event, never with a quiet 'end'. A slow reader pauses the socket.\n// Returns {abort()}: closes the connection (used when whoever asked has gone away).\n// Nothing here may throw out of an event handler: this runs inside Vetro's process.\nfunction request(opts, body, cb) {\n    body = body || bytes(0);\n    var sock = null, head = bytes(0), headDone = false, dech = null, settled = false, ended = false;\n    var expect = -1, got = 0, paused = false, blocked = false, bodyless = false;\n    var payload = new PassThrough();\n    payload.on('error', function () { /* the reader went away */ });\n    payload.on('drain', function () { blocked = false; if (paused) { paused = false; try { sock.resume(); } catch (e) { /* closed */ } } });\n    function kill() { try { if (sock) sock.destroy(); } catch (x) { /* closed */ } }\n    function complete() { if (ended) return; ended = true; try { payload.end(); } catch (e) { /* closed */ } }\n    function broken(e) { if (ended) return; ended = true; try { payload.emit('error', e); } catch (x) { /* nobody listens */ } try { payload.end(); } catch (y) { /* closed */ } }\n    var sink = { writable: true, destroyed: false, end: complete, abort: function (e) { broken(e); kill(); },\n        write: function (d) { if (!ended && !payload.write(d)) blocked = true; } };\n    function fail(e) {\n        if (settled) { broken(e instanceof Error ? e : new Error(String(e))); kill(); return; }\n        settled = true;\n        kill();\n        cb(e instanceof Error ? e : new Error(String(e)));\n    }\n    function guard(fn) { return function () { try { return fn.apply(this, arguments); } catch (e) { fail(e); } }; }\n    function feed(d) {\n        if (bodyless || ended) return;\n        if (dech) dech.write(d);\n        else if (expect >= 0) {\n            var n = Math.min(d.length, expect - got);\n            if (n > 0) sink.write(n === d.length ? d : d.slice(0, n));\n            got += n;\n            if (got >= expect) { complete(); kill(); return; }\n        } else sink.write(d);\n        if (blocked && !paused && !ended) { paused = true; try { sock.pause(); } catch (e) { /* closed */ } }\n    }\n    function closed() {\n        if (!headDone) { fail(new Error('closed before a response')); return; }\n        if (ended) return;\n        if (dech || expect >= 0) broken(new Error('response cut short'));\n        else complete();\n    }\n    try { sock = tls.connect({ host: opts.host, port: opts.port || 443, servername: opts.host }); }\n    catch (e) { setImmediate(function () { fail(e); }); return { abort: function () {} }; }\n    sock.setTimeout(opts.timeout || 30000, guard(function () {\n        if (paused) return;                                  // waiting for the reader, not for the server\n        fail(new Error('timeout talking to ' + opts.host));\n    }));\n    sock.on('error', guard(fail));\n    sock.on('secureConnect', guard(function () {\n        sock.write(buildRequest(opts, body.length));\n        if (body.length) sock.write(body);\n    }));\n    sock.on('data', guard(function (d) {\n        if (headDone) { feed(d); return; }\n        head = Buffer.concat([head, d]);\n        var parsed = null, rest = null;\n        for (;;) {\n            var i = head.indexOf('\\r\\n\\r\\n');\n            if (i < 0) { if (head.length > 4 * 1024 * 1024) fail(new Error('response head too large')); return; }\n            parsed = parseHead(head.slice(0, i).toString('binary'));\n            rest = head.slice(i + 4);\n            if (parsed.status < 100 || parsed.status > 599) { fail(new Error('not an HTTP response')); return; }\n            if (parsed.status === 101) { fail(new Error('unexpected protocol switch')); return; }\n            if (parsed.status < 200) { head = rest; continue; }       // 100 Continue, 103 Early Hints: not the answer yet\n            break;\n        }\n        headDone = true;\n        bodyless = opts.method === 'HEAD' || parsed.status === 204 || parsed.status === 304;\n        if (parsed.chunked) dech = new Dechunk(sink);\n        else expect = parsed.length;\n        settled = true;\n        cb(null, { status: parsed.status, headers: parsed.headers, body: payload });\n        if (bodyless || expect === 0) { complete(); kill(); return; }\n        if (rest.length) feed(rest);\n    }));\n    sock.on('end', guard(closed));\n    sock.on('close', guard(closed));\n    return { abort: function () { settled = true; kill(); broken(new Error('aborted')); } };   // whoever asked has gone: no callback\n}\n\n// GET host/path and collect the body (at most maxBytes). cb(err, buffer, status)\nfunction fetchBuffer(host, path, maxBytes, cb) {\n    request({ host: host, method: 'GET', path: path, headers: { host: host, 'user-agent': 'vetro-youtube-plugin' }, identity: true }, null, function (err, r) {\n        if (err) return cb(err);\n        var parts = [], size = 0, done = false;\n        function finish(e) { if (done) return; done = true; if (e) cb(e); else cb(null, Buffer.concat(parts), r.status); }\n        r.body.on('data', function (c) { size += c.length; if (size > maxBytes) { finish(new Error('response too large')); return; } parts.push(c); });\n        r.body.on('end', function () { finish(null); });\n        r.body.on('error', finish);\n    });\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { Dechunk: Dechunk, parseHead: parseHead, buildRequest: buildRequest, request: request, fetchBuffer: fetchBuffer, HOP: HOP };\n","userscript.js":"'use strict';\n// The script that is added to YouTube: TizenTube (https://github.com/reisxd/TizenTube, GPL-3.0). It blocks ads, hides Shorts,\n// skips sponsor segments with SponsorBlock's public database (https://sponsor.ajay.app) and can show DeArrow titles.\n//\n// It is NOT part of this plugin. One exact release is downloaded from npm's CDN on first use and used only when its SHA-256\n// matches the value below, so the CDN cannot change what runs inside your YouTube session. A newer release is a new\n// version of this plugin. The file is kept in the plugin’s cache folder, so it is downloaded once.\n\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar path = require('path');\nvar crypto = require('crypto');\nvar client = require('./tls-client.js');\n\nvar VERSION = '1.15.2';\nvar SHA256 = '7a092351e0e348507ef9c97da8833d5f6717de628517f5299053b3c2073f1d69';\nvar HOST = 'cdn.jsdelivr.net';\nvar URL_PATH = '/npm/@foxreis/tizentube@' + VERSION + '/dist/userScript.js';\nvar MAX_BYTES = 3 * 1024 * 1024;\n\nfunction sha256(buf) { return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(buf).digest('hex'); }\n\nfunction UserScript(dir) {\n    var file = path.join(dir, 'userscript-' + VERSION + '.js'), cached = null;\n\n    // The verified bytes, or null. Checked again on every read from disk.\n    this.load = function () {\n        if (cached) return cached;\n        try {\n            var buf = fs.readFileSync(file);\n            if (sha256(buf) === SHA256) cached = { body: buf, version: VERSION };\n        } catch (e) { /* not downloaded yet */ }\n        return cached;\n    };\n\n    // cb(err, {body, version})\n    this.ensure = function (cb) {\n        var have = this.load();\n        if (have) return cb(null, have);\n        client.fetchBuffer(HOST, URL_PATH, MAX_BYTES, function (err, buf, status) {\n            if (err) return cb(err);\n            if (status !== 200) return cb(new Error('The script download answered HTTP ' + status));\n            if (sha256(buf) !== SHA256) return cb(new Error('The downloaded script does not match the expected SHA-256: not used'));\n            try {\n                fs.writeFileSync(file + '.tmp', buf, { mode: 420 });\n                fs.renameSync(file + '.tmp', file);\n            } catch (e) { return cb(new Error('Could not save the script: ' + e.message)); }\n            cached = { body: buf, version: VERSION };\n            cb(null, cached);\n        });\n    };\n    this.forget = function () { cached = null; };\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { UserScript: UserScript, VERSION: VERSION, SHA256: SHA256, HOST: HOST, URL_PATH: URL_PATH, sha256: sha256 };\n"}}
